# Shell keys (home-manager/shell.nix)
#   Ctrl-R   history: pick a past command into the prompt
#   Ctrl-T   files: insert paths at the cursor (from rg, bat preview)
#   Alt-C    directories: cd into one (macOS terminals: Option as Meta)

# ** then Tab completes with fzf, after most commands
hx **<Tab>
cd **<Tab>
ssh **<Tab>       # hosts from ~/.ssh/config and known_hosts
kill **<Tab>      # processes

# Search syntax (space = AND)
#   abc      fuzzy
#   'abc     exact substring
#   ^abc     starts with           abc$   ends with
#   !abc     doesn't contain       !^abc  doesn't start with
#   a | b    either (OR binds tighter than AND)

# Inside fzf
#   Tab / Shift-Tab        mark / unmark (with --multi)
#   Ctrl-J/K, Ctrl-N/P     move down / up
#   Shift-Up/Down          scroll the preview

# Placeholders in --preview and --bind
#   {}  the line   {1} {2} {-1}  fields (split by --delimiter, default space)
#   {+} every marked line   {q}  the query
# Actions: become(cmd) replaces fzf, execute(cmd) runs and returns,
# reload(cmd) refreshes the list, toggle-preview
fzf --bind 'ctrl-/:toggle-preview'
